menu "Klivox IR receiver"

    config KLIVOX_IR_RX_GPIO
        int "VS1838B OUT GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 27
        help
            Choose an available input GPIO. Klivox Wired uses GPIO27 by default;
            GPIO18 is reserved for the DS18B20. Power the receiver from 3.3 V.

    config KLIVOX_IR_RX_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Capture buffer entries"
        range 1024 16384
        default 4096
        help
            Two buffers are allocated, using about four bytes per entry in
            total. Larger values need more heap, especially with Wi-Fi/BLE.

    config KLIVOX_IR_RX_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "End-of-message silence (ms)"
        range 15 130
        default 50
        help
            AC remotes can send multiple sections. Increase this if a single
            command is split into incomplete frames, as in on_off_light.

    config KLIVOX_IR_DUMP_RAW
        bool "Log raw timings for each received frame"
        default y
        help
            Prints durations in microseconds, starting with a mark. Long
            serial dumps can lose subsequent frames; press one button at a time.

endmenu
